      "writtenOn": "2026-10-21T18:45:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This could be a little flatter. Something like\n```\nrv \u003d tps_rw_source_info(...);\nif (rv) goto error;\nnew_source_info \u003d source_info;\n\nnew_source_info.present_pdp \u003d pdp;\nnew_source_info.reported_pdp \u003d pdp;\n\nif (new_source_info !\u003d source_info)\n  rv \u003d tps_rw_source_info(...);\nif (rv) goto error;\n\ntask_ucsi(...);\n\nerror:\nset_state(ERROR_RECOVERY);\nreturn;\n```\n\nThat\u0027s just mechanical. Even better would be to know all of the Source Info field values from information the EC already has. (I think we do.) Then we wouldn\u0027t need to read the existing Source Info first. We could just write it. I\u0027d probably do that unconditionally. First of all, it makes the code simpler. Secondly, we should only really be changing our PDOs if our Source Info would actually change, so I think we can presume that the update is needed.",
